This commit should address #4

## [Add producers and consumers to items](https://github.com/Zistack/Satisfactory-Optimizer/pull/7/commits/c0c68b1d1b47191218dcbb0de0d2bbc09aa0ae60)

This commit adds `produced_by` and `consumed_by` fields to the `items` dictionary, which list the recipes that produce/consume each item and the amounts needed for each. I find these fields really useful for getting a quick feel for which alternates the solver is choosing to use.

## [Report more power statistics](https://github.com/Zistack/Satisfactory-Optimizer/pull/7/commits/c3e4238627bee7beb194b21c2bfe5b2d875c2a50)

This commit adds a few more power statistics, so you can see the raw power produced, the effect of augmentation, and the raw amount consumed. To avoid clutter, these new stats are only added to the report if the factory produces power.

